A fix of our own for nsh v0.3.0's Android text layout, not (yet) upstream.

StaticLayout.Builder.obtain takes builders from a pool of three and sets most options back to their defaults, but
not useBoundsForWidth and shiftDrawingOffsetForStartOverhang (Android 15). After an EditText built a layout with
glyph bounds, the next text nsh lays out with that builder breaks by bounds too, while nsh measured it by advances:
"Your computer asks GitHub once a day." measured as one line of 566.05 px breaks before "day." in a 567 px box
whose height holds one line, and Settings shows "Your computer asks GitHub once a". Each layout now sets both.

